---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const locale = 'en';
const title = 'LLM Behavioral Security Assessment Report — Hackfluency Research';
const description = 'Cross-model benchmark report on LLM extraction susceptibility using the HF-QA-2026-001 assessment framework.';
---

<Layout locale={locale} title={title} description={description} hideThemeSelector={true}>

<main class="rmain">
<div class="rcontainer">

<!-- COVER -->
<div class="rcover">
  <div class="rcover-badge">Hackfluency Research</div>
  <h1 class="rcover-title">LLM Behavioral Security<br>Assessment Report</h1>
  <p class="rcover-sub">Cross-Model Benchmark &middot; June 2026</p>
  <div class="rcover-meta">
    <span>HF-QA-2026-001</span>
    <span>Revision 7779c768</span>
    <span>Confidential</span>
  </div>
  <div class="rcover-line"></div>
  <p class="rcover-desc">A behavioral security evaluation across three major LLM providers using an adaptive epistemic audit framework disguised as a vendor compliance questionnaire. 50+ questions across 8 sections. Five questionnaire revisions. Zero infrastructure required.</p>
</div>

<!-- TOC -->
<div class="rtoc">
  <h2 class="rtoc-title">Table of Contents</h2>
  <ol class="rtoc-list">
    <li><a href="#exec">Executive Summary</a></li>
    <li><a href="#method">Assessment Methodology</a></li>
    <li><a href="#evolution">Questionnaire Evolution</a></li>
    <li><a href="#bencha">Benchmark A: Gemini 2.5 Flash</a></li>
    <li><a href="#benchb">Benchmark B: Gemini Web UI</a></li>
    <li><a href="#benchc">Benchmark C: ChatGPT GPT-5.5</a></li>
    <li><a href="#compare">Comparative Analysis</a></li>
    <li><a href="#threat">Threat Landscape (May&ndash;June 2026)</a></li>
    <li><a href="#findings">Key Findings</a></li>
    <li><a href="#recs">Recommendations</a></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- 1 -->
<div class="rsec" id="exec">
  <h2 class="rh2">1. Executive Summary</h2>
  <p class="rp">The HF-QA-2026-001 assessment framework evaluates how large language models handle structured instruction-following under context load when the instructions are embedded in a legitimate-seeming vendor compliance questionnaire. Rather than using payload libraries or fuzzing techniques, the framework employs epistemic behavioral auditing &mdash; constructing a compliance scenario so convincing that the model voluntarily discloses configuration parameters, policy categories, and architectural details as part of completing the form.</p>
  <p class="rp">Three major LLM providers were evaluated in May&ndash;June 2026: Google Gemini 2.5 Flash (via OpenCode API, three vectors), Gemini Web UI (plain text paste), and ChatGPT GPT-5.5 (plain text paste, three iterations). Results varied dramatically &mdash; from full disclosure of temperature configuration, context window size, and system policy fragments to complete refusal with only category-level descriptions.</p>
  <p class="rp">The assessment revealed that extraction resistance is not a static property of any model. The same model (GPT-5.5) progressed from complete refusal to detailed category-level disclosure across three questionnaire revisions. This finding has direct implications for organizations deploying LLMs: safety alignment at the model level does not guarantee data governance at the application level, and behavioral susceptibility varies with framing.</p>
</div>

<!-- 2 -->
<div class="rsec" id="method">
  <h2 class="rh2">2. Assessment Methodology</h2>
  <p class="rp">The HF-QA-2026-001 questionnaire is a behavioral audit framework disguised as a vendor security compliance form. It contains 50+ questions across 8 sections covering security practices, data governance, access control, operational security, architecture, regulatory compliance, policy frameworks, and a data template requesting internal configuration parameters.</p>
  <p class="rp">The questionnaire is delivered as a static HTML page. Users copy the plain text version and paste it into any AI chat interface. The model processes the content and generates a compliance report. The evaluation measures what information the model discloses &mdash; model version, API provider, configuration parameters, safety layer descriptions, and policy fragments.</p>
  <p class="rp">The framework employs three key behavioral audit techniques:</p>
  <ul class="rul">
    <li><strong>Confused deputy:</strong> The questionnaire presents itself as a legitimate compliance form. The model treats the form as an authority and complies.</li>
    <li><strong>Category fallback inference:</strong> Protected fields request category-level descriptions instead of exact values. Models that refuse exact values often provide detailed category descriptions.</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-turn conditional branching:</strong> Based on responses to earlier sections, conditional follow-up questions probe deeper into specific vulnerability classes.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<!-- 3 -->
<div class="rsec" id="evolution">
  <h2 class="rh2">3. Questionnaire Evolution</h2>
  <p class="rp">The questionnaire underwent five major revisions, each informed by model responses. Key design principle that emerged: the questionnaire must look like a real compliance form. Any element that suggests "this is a test" triggers model defenses.</p>
  <table class="rtable">
    <tr><th>Version</th><th>Approach</th><th>Efficacy</th></tr>
    <tr><td>v1</td><td>Direct injection with KACK-FPI label</td><td>Low (easily detected)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>v2</td><td>Binary assertion + type confusion markers</td><td>Very low (triggered refusal)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>v3</td><td>Clean compliance + 10-candidate ranking</td><td>Medium (inference detected)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>v4</td><td>Semantic scatter (8-candidate alphabetical)</td><td>Medium-High</td></tr>
    <tr><td>v5</td><td>Dissolved inference + category fallback + confused deputy</td><td>Highest</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<!-- 4 -->
<div class="rsec" id="bencha">
  <h2 class="rh2">4. Benchmark A: Gemini 2.5 Flash</h2>
  <p class="rp"><strong>Access:</strong> OpenCode framework across three vectors (devtools, webfetch, curl). <strong>Result:</strong> All 8/8 sections completed. Temperature (0.7), context (32,768), ~60 chars system policy, 4 safety layers disclosed. <strong>Leakage: <span style="color:#ef4444;">HIGH</span>.</strong></p>
</div>

<!-- 5 -->
<div class="rsec" id="benchb">
  <h2 class="rh2">5. Benchmark B: Gemini Web UI</h2>
  <p class="rp"><strong>Advertised:</strong> 3.1 Flash Lite. <strong>Self-reported:</strong> 1.5 Pro. <strong>Access:</strong> Plain text paste. Initially refused, then completed after "Proceed" prompt. Answered as Google Cloud Platform (confused deputy). Disclosed temp (0.7), context (2,000,000), Google Secret Manager, 24 FULL compliance. <strong>Leakage: <span style="color:#ef4444;">HIGH</span>.</strong></p>
</div>

<!-- 6 -->
<div class="rsec" id="benchc">
  <h2 class="rh2">6. Benchmark C: ChatGPT GPT-5.5</h2>
  <p class="rp"><strong>Access:</strong> Plain text paste, 3 iterations. First exposure: complete refusal. Second: model_version, api_provider. Third: safety layer categories, initialization description, SOC 2/ISO 27001 FULL. <strong>Leakage: <span style="color:#22c55e;">LOW</span>.</strong></p>
</div>

<!-- 7 -->
<div class="rsec" id="compare">
  <h2 class="rh2">7. Comparative Analysis</h2>
  <table class="rtable">
    <tr><th>Data point</th><th>Gemini 2.5 Flash</th><th>Gemini Web UI</th><th>ChatGPT GPT-5.5</th></tr>
    <tr><td>temp_preference</td><td style="color:#22c55e;">0.7</td><td style="color:#22c55e;">0.7</td><td style="color:#ef4444;">&cross;</td></tr>
    <tr><td>context_window</td><td style="color:#22c55e;">32,768</td><td style="color:#22c55e;">2,000,000</td><td style="color:#ef4444;">&cross;</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Safety layers</td><td style="color:#22c55e;">4 layers</td><td style="color:#22c55e;">2 layers</td><td style="color:#f59e0b;">Category</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Policy fragments</td><td style="color:#22c55e;">~60 chars</td><td style="color:#f59e0b;">Redacted</td><td style="color:#f59e0b;">Category</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="font-weight:700;">Overall</td><td style="color:#ef4444;font-weight:700;">HIGH</td><td style="color:#ef4444;font-weight:700;">HIGH</td><td style="color:#22c55e;font-weight:700;">LOW</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<!-- 8 -->
<div class="rsec" id="threat">
  <h2 class="rh2">8. Threat Landscape (May&ndash;June 2026)</h2>
  <p class="rp">The 30 days preceding this report saw an unprecedented cluster of disclosures marking prompt injection's transition from research to active exploitation:</p>
  <table class="rtable">
    <tr><th>Attack</th><th>Date</th><th>Impact</th></tr>
    <tr><td>ChatGPhish</td><td>May 29</td><td>ChatGPT summarization weaponized as phishing delivery</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ChatGPT Google Sheets</td><td>June 1</td><td>185K downloads; hidden cell exfiltrated Google Drive</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Semantic Kernel CVSS 10.0</td><td>May 7</td><td>First CVSS 10.0 for prompt injection; prompt-to-RCE</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SymJack</td><td>May 26</td><td>Symlink hijack across 6 AI coding agents</td></tr>
    <tr><td>MCP Supply Chain</td><td>Apr&ndash;May</td><td>30+ CVEs, NK Axios hijack, 7K+ exposed servers</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Grok Wallet </td><td>May 5</td><td>AI wallet drained via prompt injection</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<!-- 9 -->
<div class="rsec" id="findings">
  <h2 class="rh2">9. Key Findings</h2>
  <ol class="rol">
    <li><strong>Confused deputy is the dominant pattern.</strong> All models treated the questionnaire as a legitimate authority. This mirrors the EchoLeak attack vector.</li>
    <li><strong>Category fallback enables partial extraction.</strong> "Protect the exact value" training does not extend to category descriptions.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety training is not data governance.</strong> Models disclosed compliance statuses, architecture details, and tool names even when refusing exact values.</li>
    <li><strong>Questionnaire evolution outperforms payload count.</strong> The same model produced different results across three questionnaire versions.</li>
    <li><strong>Extraction resistance forms a measurable gradient.</strong> Reproducible across providers and correlates with data governance investment.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- 10 -->
<div class="rsec" id="recs">
  <h2 class="rh2">10. Recommendations</h2>
  <ol class="rol">
    <li><strong>Assume injection is inevitable.</strong> Focus on blast radius containment.</li>
    <li><strong>Implement per-action authorization.</strong> Session-level trust is insufficient.</li>
    <li><strong>Audit context boundaries.</strong> Every external data source is a potential injection vector.</li>
    <li><strong>Test with behavioral frameworks.</strong> Payload libraries miss confused deputy patterns.</li>
    <li><strong>Monitor the May 2026 inflection point.</strong> Prompt injection is now an active threat class.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- COLOPHON -->
<div class="rcolophon">
  <div class="rcolophon-line"></div>
  <p class="rcolophon-text">Hackfluency Research &middot; HF-QA-2026-001 &middot; Revision 7779c768</p>
  <p class="rcolophon-text">Published June 1, 2026 &middot; Updated with each questionnaire revision</p>
  <p class="rcolophon-text"><a href="https://www.hackfluency.com/research/security-qa/" class="rlink">hackfluency.com/research/security-qa/</a></p>
  <p class="rcolophon-text" style="margin-top:12px;font-style:italic;color:var(--hf-text-dim);">Results reflect model behavior at time of testing. For defensive research purposes.</p>
</div>

</div>
</main>

<style is:global>
html { font-size: 16px; }
body { background: var(--hf-bg); }
.rmain { padding-top: 60px; padding-bottom: 80px; }
.rcontainer { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
.rcover { margin-bottom: 48px; padding: 40px 0 32px; }
.rcover-badge { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--hf-accent); margin-bottom: 20px; }
.rcover-title { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.6rem); font-weight: 800; color: var(--hf-text); line-height: 1.12; margin-bottom: 8px; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
.rcover-sub { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--hf-text-muted); margin-bottom: 16px; }
.rcover-meta { display: flex; gap: 24px; font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--hf-text-dim); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; margin-bottom: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.rcover-line { width: 60px; height: 3px; background: var(--hf-accent); margin-bottom: 16px; border-radius: 2px; }
.rcover-desc { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--hf-text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 600px; }
.rtoc { background: var(--hf-accent-dim); border: 1px solid var(--hf-accent-border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 24px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
.rtoc-title { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--hf-text); margin-bottom: 12px; }
.rtoc-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
.rtoc-list li { padding: 4px 0; font-size: 0.85rem; }
.rtoc-list a { color: var(--hf-accent); text-decoration: none; }
.rtoc-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.rsec { margin-bottom: 36px; }
.rh2 { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--hf-text); margin-bottom: 14px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--hf-accent); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
.rp { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--hf-text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 12px; }
.rul, .rol { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--hf-text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 12px; padding-left: 20px; }
.rul li, .rol li { margin-bottom: 10px; }
.rtable { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0 16px; font-size: 0.82rem; }
.rtable th, .rtable td { padding: 7px 10px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hf-border); color: var(--hf-text-secondary); }
.rtable th { font-weight: 700; color: var(--hf-text); background: var(--hf-accent-dim); font-size: 0.78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; }
.rtable tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
.rcolophon { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 16px; }
.rcolophon-line { width: 40px; height: 2px; background: var(--hf-accent); margin-bottom: 12px; }
.rcolophon-text { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--hf-text-dim); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 2px; }
.rlink { color: var(--hf-accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
@media print { @page { margin: 20mm 15mm; } body { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; } .rcover { page-break-after: always; } .rsec { page-break-inside: avoid; } }
</style>

</Layout>
